# ─── Demo mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When true (default), every page works with rich mock data and no backend.
# Set to "false" to connect to the real playground / control-plane / registries.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ACDP_UI_DEMO_MODE=true

# ─── Upstream services (required when demo mode is false) ────────────
# Each must be the FINAL url. The proxy refuses to relay or follow a redirect
# (it answers 502 naming the Location instead), so an `http://` base behind an
# ingress that 301s to `https://` makes a service that is up read as
# unreachable. Use the scheme and host the backend actually serves on.
PLAYGROUND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
CONTROL_PLANE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001
REGISTRY_A_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8100
REGISTRY_B_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8200

# ─── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sent as a Bearer token on every control-plane request. Upstream credential
# — never sent to the browser.
CONTROL_PLANE_API_KEY=

# Console-side operator passphrase (distinct from CONTROL_PLANE_API_KEY
# above): gates /api/proxy/* and /api/stream/* in middleware.ts behind a
# signed session cookie set by POST /api/auth/login. Unset in development,
# the gate fails OPEN (with a console warning) so the zero-setup demo keeps
# working; unset in production, the gate fails CLOSED (503) — REQUIRED in
# any production deployment that calls the real backends. There is no login
# rate-limiting (accepted tradeoff for a single-operator tool), so passphrase
# entropy is the real defense: use 4+ diceware words or 20+ random characters.
ACDP_UI_CONSOLE_PASSWORD=

# ─── Observability ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is the only Jaeger var the app reads — it's inlined into the bundle
# (the trace links are rendered client-side) and doubles as the default for
# the Jaeger URL preference in lib/stores/preferences-store.ts, which a user
# can override per-browser afterwards.
NEXT_PUBLIC_JAEGER_URL=http://localhost:16686

# ─── UI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not read by any app code directly — it's a Dockerfile build ARG
# (Dockerfile:20,23), overridden per-build by docker.yml:65 to the git ref/SHA
# so a published image can be traced to the commit that built it. Kept here
# so `docker build` from a plain checkout (without that override) still gets
# a sane default instead of an empty string.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=0.1.0
